    "title": "Scottie Scheffler learned key lesson in lone round with Tiger Woods",
    "text": "Today's Paper Erlanger Park Guide Puzzles Local News Newsletters Obituaries Opinion Legal Notices Contact Us August 20, 2025 by DOUG FERGUSON / The Associated Press × AP photo by Matt Slocum / From left, Scottie Scheffler and Tiger Woods walk down the 16th fairway at Augusta National Golf Club behind Joe LeCava, the caddie for Woods, during the final round of the Masters on Nov. 15, 2020, in Augusta, Ga. ATLANTA — Scottie Scheffler shies away from comparisons to Tiger Woods even as the numbers are starting to make such links inevitable.After all, Scheffler has been No. 1 in the Official World Golf Ranking longer than anyone since Woods. He is the first player on the PGA Tour since Woods to have five-plus wins in back-to-back years. And he comes into this week’s Tour Championship, which will decide the FedEx Cup winner for the 2025 season, with a top-10 finish in each of his past 13 tournaments played. Comments Popular Stories ‘Elevating and celebrating’: Inside the battle-tested VIP section at Erlanger Park openingChampionship-winning coach Elkins resigns at HeritageWamp attends Hamilton County school district dinner instead of Lookouts stadium openingFood Scene: The Lookouts have no shortage of options for your appetiteFood Scene: New Orleans-style restaurant set to open this spring in Chattanooga Upcoming Events",
